    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 4, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Farida Kessler-Moore, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Choledocholithiasis on MRCP with abnormal liver tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "Procedure: The duodenoscope was advanced to the major papilla, which appeared normal."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "Deep biliary cannulation was achieved with a sphincterotome and a guidewire."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "Cholangiogram: the bile duct was dilated to 12 mm with three filling defects (stones)."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "A biliary sphincterotomy was performed with blended current, without bleeding."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "Three stones, the largest 9 mm, were extracted from the bile duct with an extraction balloon."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "An occlusion cholangiogram showed no residual filling defects."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "Fluoroscopy images were interpreted separately by the radiology service."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "Impression: Choledocholithiasis; biliary sphincterotomy and complete balloon stone extraction."
    }
